## Answer

**Redis first got the Streams data type (with commands like `XADD`) in commit `79866a636` — "Streams: 12 commits squashed into the initial Streams implementation."** (authored by antirez, dated Wed Aug 30 12:40:27 2017 +0200).

This is the very first commit in the repository's history to introduce `src/t_stream.c` and `src/stream.h`, and it registers `XADD` as a server command and implements it:

Commit message:
```
Streams: 12 commits squashed into the initial Streams implementation.
```

Diff excerpt from `src/server.c` (command table registration):
```c
+    {"xadd",xaddCommand,-4,"wmF",0,NULL,1,1,1,0,0},
```

Diff excerpt from `src/t_stream.c` (the command implementation):
```c
+void xaddCommand(client *c) {
+    if ((c->argc % 2) == 1) {
+        addReplyError(c,"wrong number of arguments for XADD");
+        return;
+    }
+
+    /* Lookup the stream at key. */
+    robj *o;
+    stream *s;
+    if ((o = streamTypeLookupWriteOrCreate(c,c->argv[1])) == NULL) return;
+    s = o->ptr;
+
+    /* Append using the low level function and return the ID. */
+    streamID id;
+    streamAppendItem(s,c->argv+2,(c->argc-2)/2,&id);
+    sds reply = sdscatfmt(sdsempty(),"+%U.%U\r\n",id.ms,id.seq);
+    addReplySds(c,reply);
+
+    signalModifiedKey(c->db,c->argv[1]);
+    notifyKeyspaceEvent(NOTIFY_HASH,"xadd",c->argv[1],c->db->id);
+    server.dirty++;
+}
```

I confirmed via `git log --oneline --all -- src/t_stream.c src/stream.h` that this is the oldest commit touching these files (its direct parent, `045d65c3a`, has no stream-related code), and checked the immediate follow-on commits in the reachable history (`100d43c1a` "assign value of 6 to OBJ_STREAM...", `485014cc7` "Streams: RDB saving.", etc.) confirming this squashed commit is where the feature branch begins in this repo's history. No files were modified during this investigation.
